            <ArticleTitle>Identification of the anaerobic threshold using double product in patients with coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>360-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This study compared the ventilatory threshold with the double-product break point in 104 patients with cardiovascular disease during ramp treadmill testing. The high correlation (r = 0.81) between the double-product break point and the ventilatory threshold, even in patients taking beta blockers, suggests the former method is a viable noninvasive alternative for identifying the anaerobic threshold in patients with cardiovascular disease, particularly when expired gas analysis is not appropriate or available.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
